{
  "id": "rotating_bodies___stress",
  "title": "Rotating Bodies - Stress",
  "description": "Stress in rotating disc and ring bodies. Calculate stress in rotating discs and rings based on angular velocity, dimensions, and material density.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Stress in a Rotating Disc\n\nStress in a rotating disc can be calculated as:\n\n**σz = ω² r² ρ / 3**\n\nOr alternatively:\n\n**σz = v² ρ / 3**\n\nOr using RPM:\n\n**σz = (2π n / 60)² r² ρ / 3**\n\nWhere:\n- σz = stress (Pa, N/m²)\n- ω = angular velocity (rad/s)\n- r = radius of disc (m)\n- ρ = density (kg/m³)\n- v = tangential velocity (m/s)\n- n = revolutions per minute (rpm)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "body_type",
          "label": "Body Type",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Rotating Disc",
              "value": "disc"
            },
            {
              "label": "Rotating Ring",
              "value": "ring"
            }
          ],
          "defaultValue": "disc"
        },
        {
          "id": "angular_velocity",
          "label": "Angular Velocity (ω)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "rad/s",
          "defaultValue": 100
        },
        {
          "id": "radius",
          "label": "Radius (r)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "outer_radius",
          "label": "Outer Radius (r₁)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 0.5
        },
        {
          "id": "inner_radius",
          "label": "Inner Radius (r₂)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 0.3
        },
        {
          "id": "mean_radius",
          "label": "Mean Radius (r)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "m",
          "defaultValue": 0.4
        },
        {
          "id": "density",
          "label": "Density (ρ)",
          "type": "number",
          "unit": "kg/m³",
          "defaultValue": 7850
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "stress_disc",
          "label": "Stress in Disc",
          "formula": "inputs.angular_velocity^2 * inputs.radius^2 * inputs.density / 3",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "stress_ring",
          "label": "Stress in Ring",
          "formula": "inputs.angular_velocity^2 * inputs.density * (inputs.outer_radius^2 + inputs.outer_radius * inputs.inner_radius + inputs.inner_radius^2) / 3",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "stress_ring_thin",
          "label": "Stress in Thin Ring",
          "formula": "inputs.angular_velocity^2 * inputs.density * inputs.mean_radius^2",
          "unit": "Pa",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Stress in a Rotating Ring\n\nStress in a rotating ring can be calculated as:\n\n**σz = ω² ρ (r₁² + r₁r₂ + r₂²) / 3**\n\nWhere:\n- r₁ = outer radius of ring (m)\n- r₂ = inner radius of ring (m)\n\nFor a thin ring, the equation simplifies to:\n\n**σz = ω² ρ r²**\n\nWhere:\n- r = mean radius of ring (m)"
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Material",
        "Density (kg/m³)",
        "Typical Design Stress (MPa)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Aluminum alloy",
          2700,
          "—"
        ],
        [
          "Birch plywood",
          700,
          30
        ],
        [
          "Composite carbon fiber - 40% epoxy",
          1550,
          750
        ],
        [
          "E-glass fiber - 40% epoxy",
          1900,
          250
        ],
        [
          "Kevlar fiber - 40% epoxy",
          1400,
          1000
        ],
        [
          "Maraging steel",
          8000,
          900
        ],
        [
          "Titanium Alloy",
          4500,
          650
        ],
        [
          "Super paper",
          1100,
          "—"
        ],
        [
          "S-glass fiber/epoxy",
          1900,
          350
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}